{
  "source": "Prompts/tokens-1.mp4",
  "duration": 207.331,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 6.54,
      "text": "Computers process all information purely as numbers, but as humans, we input text and language."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.16,
      "end": 11.84,
      "text": "When you type a prompt, how does the AI actually bridge that gap to read your words?"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.44,
      "end": 18.76,
      "text": "The system relies on a background process called tokenization, which breaks your text down into manageable chunks."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.44,
      "end": 26.54,
      "text": "Without this invisible translation step, large language models would be completely incapable of processing or generating human language."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.54,
      "end": 32.1,
      "text": "It is a common assumption that AI models simply memorize a massive dictionary of whole words,"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.4,
      "end": 36.56,
      "text": "but operating that way would require a highly inefficient amount of processing power."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.1,
      "end": 40.16,
      "text": "Instead, the model relies on subword building blocks."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.74,
      "end": 44.28,
      "text": "This graphic demonstrates the baseline rule using the word unbelievable."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.04,
      "end": 52.5,
      "text": "Rather than memorizing it as one long item, the AI splits the word into three distinct pieces, un, belie, and vable."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.5,
      "end": 58.02,
      "text": "These fragmented chunks are valuable because they can be reused across the model's entire vocabulary."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.72,
      "end": 64.84,
      "text": "The un-piece is recycled to build completely different words, like unmatchable and unusual."
    },
    {
      "start": 65.62,
      "end": 70.52,
      "text": "By recycling these small building blocks instead of storing every possible word in existence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 71.2,
      "end": 75.2,
      "text": "the AI radically reduces the processing power needed to handle human language."
    },
    {
      "start": 75.98,
      "end": 78.94,
      "text": "Simply cutting a word into pieces isn't the final step."
    },
    {
      "start": 78.94,
      "end": 83.94,
      "text": "To run its calculations, the AI must convert those text chunks into numbers."
    },
    {
      "start": 84.68,
      "end": 91.2,
      "text": "When you read cat, you instantly picture the animal, but the tokenizer assigns a numerical identifier to that text."
    },
    {
      "start": 91.72,
      "end": 95.66,
      "text": "Here, cat converts into 4719, a token ID."
    },
    {
      "start": 96.28,
      "end": 101.3,
      "text": "That number identifies the token, but contains no meaning or understanding of what a cat is."
    },
    {
      "start": 101.7,
      "end": 103.3,
      "text": "It's strictly a dictionary coordinate."
    },
    {
      "start": 103.3,
      "end": 109.6,
      "text": "The actual deep understanding of the text happens much deeper inside the AI's vast neural network."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.26,
      "end": 114.82,
      "text": "The text we type into an AI isn't limited to perfectly spelled dictionary words."
    },
    {
      "start": 115.52,
      "end": 118.48,
      "text": "Prompts are filled with names, symbols, and irregular formatting."
    },
    {
      "start": 119.1,
      "end": 122.96,
      "text": "This list demonstrates how different types of text yield different tulp and pounce."
    },
    {
      "start": 124.06,
      "end": 131.0,
      "text": "Basketball splits into two obvious pieces, but a newer term like chat GPT fractures into three less intuitive chunks."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.62,
      "end": 132.96,
      "text": "Tokenization is absolute."
    },
    {
      "start": 133.5,
      "end": 137.96,
      "text": "Even an empty leading space or a heart emoji gets its own distinct numerical ID."
    },
    {
      "start": 138.76,
      "end": 143.48,
      "text": "Pause the video for a second and guess how many tokens a complex string like a web address might generate."
    },
    {
      "start": 144.0,
      "end": 149.32,
      "text": "If you look at row 5, you'll see the punctuation and domain structure shatter into eight unique identifiers."
    },
    {
      "start": 150.04,
      "end": 157.58,
      "text": "Absolutely every keystroke, no matter how strange, must be mathematically mapped into an ID to exist in the AI's computational space."
    },
    {
      "start": 157.58,
      "end": 162.86,
      "text": "We can trace the entire journey of a prompt by mapping it out here as a strict sequential pipeline."
    },
    {
      "start": 163.54,
      "end": 165.68,
      "text": "This diagram shows the process in three phases."
    },
    {
      "start": 166.42,
      "end": 167.82,
      "text": "Step 1, you type a message."
    },
    {
      "start": 168.38,
      "end": 172.56,
      "text": "Step 2, the tokenizer intercepts that text and fractures it into reusable chunks."
    },
    {
      "start": 173.12,
      "end": 176.8,
      "text": "Step 3, the system locates and outputs the final numerical token IDs."
    },
    {
      "start": 177.38,
      "end": 182.18,
      "text": "This sequence is the invisible gateway for every prompt processed by modern AI models."
    },
    {
      "start": 182.78,
      "end": 185.7,
      "text": "This brings us back to the familiar screen you use every day."
    },
    {
      "start": 185.7,
      "end": 189.26,
      "text": "While this feels exactly like natural human communication,"
    },
    {
      "start": 189.94,
      "end": 194.92,
      "text": "the tokenization engine is relentlessly churning your text into numbers in the background to make it all work."
    },
    {
      "start": 195.54,
      "end": 197.76,
      "text": "You use words. AI uses numbers."
    },
    {
      "start": 198.48,
      "end": 203.62,
      "text": "This conversion is the essential first step that allows AI to process the complexity of human language."
    }
  ],
